From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:23:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] minimize: side panel items with badges and a hover card

On a left or right panel the taskbar showed upstream's window
thumbnails, without tab counts, unread counts or a second line.

Each window is now a square item with its app icon and the focused
window's background. A pin at the top right marks an app pinned to a
workspace, as on the top/bottom taskbar. A badge at the bottom right
shows the unread count (red) or, without one, the tab or item count of
the second line (grey); counts above 99 show as "99+". Windows that do
not fit go to the overflow popup as the same items.

Hovering an item opens a card beside the panel (right of a left panel,
left of a right panel): the icon, the title and the second line above
the live preview. With the preview turned off in the options file the
card shows only its header and nothing is captured.

Tab files, unread counts, media players and pins are now read on side
panels too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

